### 4. Smallest Correct Native & Renderer Fix

#### Native Fix (`src-tauri/src/lib.rs`)
1. Re-assign `Window -> Close Window` to `CmdOrCtrl+Shift+W` (standard macOS tabbed application behavior, e.g., Safari / Terminal / VS Code) or use `MenuItemBuilder` with `CmdOrCtrl+Shift+W` so `CmdOrCtrl+W` uniquely maps to `File -> Close Tab`.
2. Keep `File -> Close Tab` with accelerator `CmdOrCtrl+W` emitting `"menu_close_tab"`.

```rust
// src-tauri/src/lib.rs
let close_window = MenuItemBuilder::with_id("window.close", "Close Window")
    .accelerator("CmdOrCtrl+Shift+W")
    .build(app)?;

let window_menu = SubmenuBuilder::new(app, "Window")
    .minimize()
    .item(&PredefinedMenuItem::maximize(app, None)?)
    .separator()
    .item(&close_window)
    .build()?;
```
*(In `on_menu_event`, `"window.close"` can call `window.close()?` if explicitly invoked).*

#### Renderer Bridge Fix (`ui/src/lib/tauri.ts` & `ui/src/App.tsx`)
1. Add `onCloseTabMenu` in `ui/src/lib/tauri.ts`:
```ts
export async function onCloseTabMenu(handler: () => void): Promise<UnlistenFn> {
  return listen<void>("menu_close_tab", () => handler());
}
```
2. Subscribe to `onCloseTabMenu` in `ui/src/App.tsx`:
```ts
useEffect(() => {
  let unlisten: (() => void) | null = null;
  let cancelled = false;
  void onCloseTabMenu(() => {
    const activeTabId = stateRef.current.layout.activeTabId;
    if (activeTabId) handleCloseTab(activeTabId);
  }).then((dispose) => {
    if (cancelled) dispose();
    else unlisten = dispose;
  });
  return () => {
    cancelled = true;
    unlisten?.();
  };
}, [handleCloseTab]);
```

#### Preservation of Mobile & Remote Web Clients
* Web/remote clients (`ui/src/remote/RemoteApp.tsx`, `ui/src/components/MobileKeyDock.tsx`) run in environments without Tauri native menus.
* `useShortcuts` DOM keydown listener in `ui/src/lib/shortcuts.ts` and UI close buttons continue to handle `Cmd+W`/`Ctrl+W` and mobile touch events directly into `closeTab(tabId)`. The Tauri menu IPC listener is strictly additive for native desktop execution.

